[objrel-first-to-fire] VERDICT: BOUNDARY
BOUNDARY -- OBJREL did not recover 6-seed-blind (1/6 overall, 1/3 blind; need >=5/6 AND all blind); CANONICAL regressed with first-to-fire on (the see-saw survived the latency read); first-to-fire is NOT load-bearing (the summed-argmax read at the same floor did not collapse objrel -> the recovery is the floor-lowering, not the latency code); the scrambled-label control did NOT collapse (the read is a position/heterogeneity artifact). [dt PRE-CHECK: the correct ens's first spike was strictly earliest on 0/6 seeds -- where 0, RANK-1 is dt-BLOCKED (the ens tie on the first step even at the swept floor, so latency carries no differential).] The reservoir FEATURE robustly encodes objrel (a shift-invariant linear argmax solves it 100%), so it is NOT the Mikulasch-Priesemann wall -- it is the seed-adaptive spiking-read frontier. RANK-1 latency is a genuinely different code from the exhausted pedestal-REMOVAL family (subtraction/division), but on this point-neuron f-I at dt=1.0 the ens either saturate (tie) or under-fire. An HONEST characterization; NO anti-cheat was weakened to force a GO. THE INDICATED NEXT MECHANISM: a SIGNED ON/OFF (+/-) read (negative Ws rows via an inhibitory relay), which fits THROUGH the spiking deploy so the f-I nonlinearity + WTA ignition-order are INSIDE the error.
